===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|arounde|around, arounde}}, from {{m|enm|a-}} (from {{inh|en|ang|a-||on, at}}) + {{inh|en|enm|round||circle, round}} borrowed from French, equivalent to {{prefix|en|a|round|id1=on}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|aroond}}, {{m|sco|aroon||around}}. Displaced earlier {{cog|enm|umbe}}, {{m|enm|embe||around}} (from {{cog|ang|ymbe||around}}).

